__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Corpora and derived artifacts: large, regenerable, never versioned.
#
# 🔴 ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is load-bearing. An unanchored
# `data/` matches ANY directory named `data` at any depth. It did, for both
# `src/rsr/data/` (the synthetic-corpus package, gauntlet 2.5) and
# `third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/` (five files of the pinned
# reference). Both were invisible from the scaffold commit until 2026-09-17:
# ignored files do not show in `git status`, `git add -A` skips them silently,
# and every local test passes because the files are on disk. A fresh clone had
# `tests/test_synthetic.py` with nothing to import, and a vendored tree that did
# not match the pin.
#
# `tests/test_repo_integrity.py` now checks the class, not the two instances.
/data/
/outputs/
*.ckpt
*.pt

# ...but the measurement ledgers are evidence, not output.
#
# `/runs/` correctly ignores checkpoints (binary, large, regenerable) and
# heartbeats (per-step, chatty). It also ignored `runs/<id>/ledger.json`, which is
# the artefact the overnight protocol requires **every reported number to trace
# to** -- so a cycle's evidence could not be committed and a claim had nothing
# durable behind it. Un-ignore the ledgers and the writeups only; the directory
# itself must stay ignored or `git add -A` sweeps in the .pt files.
# Note the form: `/runs/**` ignores the CONTENTS, and `!/runs/**/` re-includes the
# directories. Ignoring `/runs/` itself would make the negations below dead letters
# -- git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a re-include under one can
# never match. That is exactly the trap this rule was in.
/runs/**
!/runs/**/
!/runs/**/ledger.json
!/runs/**/RESULTS.md
!/runs/**/walls.json
!/runs/**/baseline.json

# Belt and braces: the source packages are never ignorable, whatever pattern
# comes back. Scoped to sources so `__pycache__/` above still applies.
!src/rsr/data/
!src/rsr/data/*.py
!third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/
!third_party/ThoughtGestaltCode/tg/data/*.py

# Golden tensors ARE versioned (tests/fixtures/*.npz) -- they are the external
# claim test_fidelity.py rests on. See ADR-0002.

# The per-run test census written by tests/conftest.py (gauntlet 1.3).
test-count.json
